====== Dragino MS12 ======

{{section>meta:infobox:432_warning#infobox_for_dataentries&noheader&nofooter&noeditbutton}}

The [[http://www.dragino.com|Dragino MS12]] is based on an Atheros system-on-a-chip (SoC). It has a MIPS 4K processor, 8meg flash, and 32meg ram.  Unlike most home routers, it also has 6 ESD shielded inputs, for connecting to any sort of sensor, and connectors for a daughterboard, that has access to the sensor inputs, and to the MIPS serial port, and some GPIOs that can be used as a SPI port.  It is sold as an OEM device or offshore development kit, and comes with openWRT loaded, so you should have no difficulty using it. :)

{{:media:dragino:dpp_0004.png?0x200}} {{:media:dragino:dpp_0008.png?0x200|MS12 with Flukso Sensor Board}}

At retail, you can get one of these as a [[http://www.flukso.net/|Flukso Fluksometer]], for home power measurement, or from [[http://www.nodalis.es/|Nodalis]], where they are used as part of voip mesh networks.

===== Hardware =====
^ Architecture     | MIPS 4K                           |
^ Vendor           | //n/a//                           |
^ Bootloader       | RedBoot                           |
^ System-On-Chip   | Atheros AR2317                    |
^ CPU Speed        | 180 MHz                           |
^ Flash size       | 8 MiB                             |
^ RAM              | 16 MiB/ changed to 32MB in v1.0   |
^ Wireless         | Integrated Atheros 802.11b/g      |
^ Ethernet         | 1x RJ45                           |
^ USB              | No                                |
^ Serial           | Yes                               |
^ SPI              | simulated by GPIO                 |
^ JTAG             | No                                |

  * 12V power supply
  * Antenna
  * SPI-Bus
  * External ESD shielded inputs
  * daughterboard connector for personal projects (Arduino, avr, PIC etc.)


As an atheros board, the notes on [[toh:abicom::freedom_cpe|Freedom CPE]] and [[toh:fon::fonera|Fonera]] are very relevant, and much more detailed.


